  "generated_text": "To determine the probability that the line connecting two randomly chosen vertices of a regular dodecahedron lies inside the dodecahedron, we need to carefully analyze the structure and properties of the dodecahedron.\n\n### Step-by-Step Analysis:\n\n1. **Vertices and Edges of the Dodecahedron:**\n   - A regular dodecahedron has 20 vertices and 30 edges.\n\n2. **Total Number of Vertex Pairs:**\n   - The number of ways to choose 2 vertices out of 20 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{20}{2} \\):\n     \\[\n     \\binom{20}{2} = \\frac{20 \\times 19}{2} = 190\n     \\]\n\n3. **Edges of the Dodecahedron:**\n   - A regular dodecahedron has 30 edges.\n\n4. **Edges and Faces:**\n   - Each face of the dodecahedron is a regular pentagon, and each edge of the dodecahedron is shared by two faces.\n   - The dodecahedron has 12 faces, and each face has 5 edges, but each edge is counted twice (once per face), so the total number of edges is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{12 \\times 5}{2} = 30\n     \\]\n\n5. **Edges Inside the Dodecahedron:**\n   - The edges of the dodecahedron are the only edges that lie entirely within the solid structure of the dodecahedron.\n   - Therefore, all 30 edges of the dodecahedron are inside the dodecahedron.\n\n6. **Probability Calculation:**\n   - The probability that a randomly chosen line segment connecting two vertices lies inside the dodecahedron is the ratio of the number of edges inside the dodecahedron to the total number of vertex pairs:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\text{Number of edges inside the dodecahedron}}{\\text{Total number of vertex pairs}} = \\frac{30}{190} = \\frac{3}{19}\n     \\]\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3}{19}}\n\\]",
